# The SITL params every SwathKeeper flight needs, for use with `sim_vehicle.py --add-param-file`:
# AP_DDS (the ROS 2 /ap/* bridge) over UDP, plus the ADR-006 mission-resume assumption.
#
# --- AP_DDS ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Mirrors ArduPilot's own default DDS-enablement param file
# Tools/ros2/ardupilot_sitl/config/default_params/dds_udp.parm at the pinned SHA
# (9895756d874ec9128d50918f6747a83706f4e221 -- see CLAUDE.md "Pinned commit SHAs"), which is what
# ardupilot_gz_bringup's iris.launch.py loads by default. We load it explicitly here because this
# project's bringup deliberately does NOT use that launch file (it hardcodes its own world path --
# see sim/README.md "Launching the world" / docs/runbooks/SIM_BRINGUP.md for why), so nothing else in our
# flow sets these params for us.
#
# Deliberately does NOT also load ardupilot_gz_bringup's dds_use_ns.parm (DDS_USE_NS=1): that adds
# a "/v<SYSID_THISMAV>" segment to every topic/service name (e.g. /ap/v1/pose/filtered). We're
# single-vehicle, so we keep the plain /ap/<name> form already documented and expected in
# docs/runbooks/SIM_BRINGUP.md and docs/DECISIONS.md's AP_DDS interface-lock entry.
DDS_ENABLE 1
DDS_UDP_PORT 2019

# --- Mission resume (ADR-006) ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0 = RESUME the mission at the item it was on when AUTO was left; 1 = RESTART from item 1.
# The avoidance executor takes AUTO -> GUIDED -> one setpoint -> AUTO on every encounter, and its
# resume claim ("continues the lawnmower from the waypoint it was flying to") is ArduPilot's, not
# ours: ModeAuto::init calls AP_Mission::start_or_resume(), which resumes unless MIS_RESTART == 1.
# At 1 every dodge would re-fly the field from lane 1 and the coverage ledger would book that as
# flown coverage. Confirmed live 2026-08-05 (Week-3 Gate 3, docs/archive/WEEK3_VALIDATION.md).
# Pinned here 2026-08-25 (ADR-016): it had only ever been TYPED at the MAVProxy prompt, so a
# skipped line silently changed what a flight meant. The recipe still types it -- belt and braces
# for a hand-started SITL that forgot --add-param-file; this file is the pin.
MIS_RESTART 0
